## 2️⃣ Using the SoundCloud Widget API (custom UI)

If you want a custom play button, volume slider, or need to react when a track ends, use the widget API.

### Step‑by‑step

1. **Add the iframe** (same as above, but give it an `id` so you can reference it):

```html
<div id="sc-player">
  <iframe
      id="sc-widget"
      width="100%"
      height="166"
      scrolling="no"
      frameborder="no"
      allow="autoplay"
      src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/TRACK_ID&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&visual=false">
  </iframe>
</div>
```

2. **Load the Widget JavaScript** (once, preferably in the `<head>` or just before `</body>`):

```html
<script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>
```

3. **Control the player with JavaScript**:

```html
<script>
  // Wait for the iframe to load
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var iframeElement   = document.getElementById('sc-widget');
    var widget          = SC.Widget(iframeElement);

